  "overview": {
    "en": "Murray Gell-Mann was an American theoretical physicist who won the 1969 Nobel Prize in Physics for his classification of subatomic particles and the discovery of quarks. He introduced the concept of strangeness and developed the Eightfold Way classification scheme.",
